The '''2024–25 season''' was the 55th season in the history of [[Paris Saint-Germain FC|Paris Saint-Germain]], and the club's 51st consecutive season in the [[Ligue 1|French top flight]]. The club participated in [[2024–25 Ligue 1|Ligue 1]], the [[2024–25 Coupe de France|Coupe de France]], the [[2024 Trophée des Champions|Trophée des Champions]], the [[2024–25 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]], and the newly expanded [[2025 FIFA Club World Cup|FIFA Club World Cup]] for the first time.

This was the club's first season since [[2016–17 Paris Saint-Germain FC season|2016–17]] without record goalscorer [[Kylian Mbappé]], who left the Parisian side to join European champions [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]], and the first since [[2014–15 Paris Saint-Germain FC season|2014–15]] without [[Layvin Kurzawa]], who also departed after his contract expired.

PSG achieved their best season in club history, securing the Ligue 1 and Coupe de France titles before defeating [[Inter Milan]] by a record [[2025 UEFA Champions League final|5–0 scoreline]] to become the second team from France to win the Champions League–after [[Olympique de Marseille|Marseille]] in [[1993 UEFA Champions League final|1993]]–as well as the first French side to win a [[Treble (association football)#Continental trebles|continental treble]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0251-0e99b1ba85da-ec8053dc0a29-1000--paris-complete-the-11th-domestic-league-domestic-cup-and-e/ |title=Paris complete the 11th domestic league, domestic cup and European Cup/UEFA Champions League treble |publisher=UEFA |date=31 May 2025 |access-date=31 May 2025}}</ref>

